{"reference":"Jeremiah 42","book":"Jeremiah","chapter":42,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"In the Surrounding Narrative","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Jeremiah 42 belongs to the book’s larger narrative of Judah’s crisis under Babylonian domination, including Jerusalem’s destruction, Gedaliah, and a flight to Egypt. That wider setting gives weight to the remnant’s request for guidance about whether to remain in the land or go to Egypt.","provenance_refs":["reader_path_jeremiah_042_369826324d58b9882d384f70"],"confidence":"medium","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}